drill.prompt:
A fresh process on glibc runs the five lines below. For each line, write as a comment the system call it makes, if any. Assume the default thresholds, and that the program keeps every block's address.

```c
char *a = malloc(64);
char *b = malloc(64 * 1024);
char *c = malloc(512 * 1024);
free(c);
char *d = malloc(512 * 1024);
```
